Gigadrone was used alongside [[Venomaster]] by [[Unnamed Suit 053]], from [[The Organization]] now led by [[Mr. Wilder]] to ambush and destroy the [[Huntik Foundation|Huntik]] team. It fought [[Dante Vale]] and his [[Caliban]] but was defeated by [[Lok|Lok's]] [[Raijin the Thunderbolt]]. Three more Gigadrone [[Titans]] were later used by Mr. Wilder's Suits outside the waterfall cave in an attempt to stop Dante Vale and [[Zhalia Moon]]. After fighting [[Gar-Ghoul]] and [[Elf King Oberon]], the final Gigadrone was defeated by the newly [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird's]] 'Sword Strike' ability. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Two Gigadrones were used by Mr. Wilder's  Suits outside the [[Crystal Caves]] to ambush the Huntik team and destroy their tents. One pursued Lok and [[Cherit]] and chased them through the woods. Despite catching up, Gigadrone was defeated by [[Kipperin|Powerbonded Kipperin's]] 'Light Burst' ability. Two more were later seen accompanying the Organization boats to [[Avalon]]. {{source|Knight of the Willblade}}

Gigadrone was summoned by [[Unnamed Suit 055]] to fight alongside [[Venomaster]] against Dante's [[Metagolem]] but was defeated by [[Lane|Lane's]] [[Wildwood Druid]] when [[Lucas Casterwill]] and his team intervened. {{source|Chasing Void}}

Gigadrone was summoned personally by [[Mr. Wilder]] to fight Zhalia's [[Januseea the Gatekeeper]]. It fought and defeated [[Januseea the Gatekeeper|Januseea]] but was defeated by Lok's [[Baselaird|Powerbonded Baselaird]]. {{source|The Blood Spiral}}

Mr. Wilder attempted to summon Gigadrone against [[Breaker|Powerbonded Breaker]] but he was stopped by [[Grier]]. {{source|An Ally from the Organization}}
